# Where Link has proven what a list holds, the walk writes `CheckProof source=Contents [isLeftToTestBehind]` in front of the test that asks in full. That check has no code: the test behind it is the check. It was not
# among the operations of turns laid out, so an operation without code shut every loop over a list of the file out of the row. The loop is built twice (the list's storage is asked in front): both builds are laid out.
# RUN(EVENT): compile UnrolledLoopsEmitted mechanisms=all
# EVENT: statistic UnrolledLoopsEmitted 2
# RUN(WALK): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# WALK: = CheckProof {{*}} source=Contents [isLeftToTestBehind]
# -- source: main.cjs
